window.docContents[48].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Session.StatementIdsModel/#file-Computational___Specifications___Session___StatementIdsModel":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Session › StatementIdsModel.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 19 of 67 lines trusted trust banner B2, trusted: definitions used by the statement source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nSession parameters at arbitrary identity keys and the leaked-pre-key session schemeTrusted: definitions used by the statement. The theorems of Computational/Theorems/ use idsOf, paramsIdsWithSpqr and sessionSchemeFixedSpk. The statements SessionSecureIds, SessionSecureUIds, SessionSecureSpkIds and SessionSecureSpkIdsWithSpqr, and paramsIds, are in Computational/Proofs/SpecLemmas/Session/StatementIdsModel.lean, checked by Lean. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.Defines session parameters for caller-chosen identity keys idA, idB (which enter the wire MACs) and the leaked-pre-key session scheme sessionSchemeFixedSpk, where Bob's signed-pre-key scalar s is fixed externally while the remaining initial keys are sampled via SampledSessionKey.\n\n\n\nSession parameters\n\ndef paramsIdsWithSpqrL43–49 ↗#Session parameters for SPQR instance spqr and party identity keys idA, idB, with protoSignalCodec and serialized UUID party addresses (uuidTryParse).\n\ndef idsOfL51–54 ↗#Assigns identity key idA to .A and idB to .B.\n\nLeaked-pre-key session scheme\n\ndef sessionSchemeFixedSpkL58–65 ↗#Single-session SMSchemeR with Bob's signed-pre-key coins fixed to s, keyed by SampledSessionKey via initKeysOfSampled s with plaintexts fitted to ℓ bytes.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Session/StatementIdsModel.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Session.StatementIdsModel/#file-Computational___Specifications___Session___StatementIdsModel"}});